---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="About the Kvantiq Directory — the open European quantum computing ecosystem directory.">
  <article class="prose prose-gray mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">About Kvantiq Directory</h1>

    <div class="summary mt-4" role="doc-abstract">
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        Kvantiq Directory is a curated, open directory of the European quantum computing ecosystem.
        We catalog companies, benchmarks, use cases, challenges, and resources — starting with
        the Nordics and DACH regions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Why this directory?</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700">
        Europe has invested over EUR 10 billion in quantum computing through combined EU and national
        funding programs. There are 150+ quantum computing companies across the continent, yet no
        single directory focused on the European ecosystem exists. Kvantiq Directory fills that gap.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Our scope</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700">
        We focus on hybrid quantum-classical and quantum-AI applications — the intersection where
        quantum computing meets real-world industry problems. Our geographic focus starts with the
        Nordics (Denmark, Finland, Sweden) and DACH (Germany, Austria, Switzerland) regions, expanding
        to cover all of Europe.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Ethics policy</h2>
      <ul class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>European-first, open-source preferred.</strong> We prioritize European companies and open-source projects.</li>
        <li><strong>No visitor data exploitation.</strong> No third-party tracking pixels, no Google Analytics, no Facebook pixels.</li>
        <li><strong>Ethical advertising only.</strong> No Google AdSense — only privacy-respecting, contextual ad networks.</li>
        <li><strong>Allowlist approach.</strong> Companies are listed based on alignment with open science, European tech sovereignty, and democratic values.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Submit a listing</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-gray-700">
        Know a company, benchmark, or resource that should be listed? <a href="/submit/" class="text-indigo-700 hover:underline">Submit a listing</a> and we'll review it.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
